
OJA FERTILITY
Master Question Taxonomy
Reproductive Health, IVF, Women's & Male Fertility — Questions Indian Couples Actually Ask

1000 questions across 50 categories
Prepared for the OJA Knowledge Hub — Patient-facing content planning
Internal working document · July 2026
 How to Use This Taxonomy
This document maps the questions Indian couples realistically search for and ask doctors — in their own words, including colloquial phrasing, myths, and culturally specific concerns — organized into a category structure suitable for a knowledge hub's information architecture (IA).
Suggested next steps:
●	Use section headers (A, B, C…) as top-level knowledge hub categories or tags.
●	Prioritize content creation using search-volume/relevance data before writing answers for all 821 questions.
●	Route medically sensitive myth-busting questions (Section AC) through clinical review before publishing, given cultural sensitivity.
●	Cross-reference each question against your 6 vetted sources (FOGSI, ASRM, WHO, ISAR, HFEA, Urology Care Foundation) to ensure every published answer is source-backed.
●	Flag India-specific legal questions (Sections X, Z) for review against the latest ART/Surrogacy Act amendments before publishing, since regulations evolve.
●	Treat Section AC (Myths & Taboos) and AD (Emotional Wellbeing) with particular care in tone — these carry real emotional weight for users.
